     Strings of the reduced-motion row on the Appearance page of Settings (issue #174). patches/sidebar/0002 gives each
     one to the settings page under the name tests/test_design_tokens.py checks. -->
<grit-part>
  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_AERIE_MOTION_REDUCE" desc="Label of the drop-down on the Appearance page that decides whether Aerie reduces the motion of its own interface.">
    Reduce motion
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_AERIE_MOTION_REDUCE_DESC" desc="Line under the reduce motion drop-down. It says what reduced motion changes and that web pages and the browser's other animations are not changed.">
    Aerie's own animations use short fades and no sliding or scaling. Web pages and the animations of the rest of the browser do not change.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_AERIE_MOTION_REDUCE_SYSTEM" desc="Option of the reduce motion drop-down: reduce motion only when the operating system asks for it. This is the default.">
    Follow the system setting
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_AERIE_MOTION_REDUCE_ON" desc="Option of the reduce motion drop-down: always reduce motion, whatever the operating system says.">
    Always reduce motion
  </message>
</grit-part>
